    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you, but it feels like you're saying that focusing on biology is somehow less \"healthy\" or \"compassionate\" than focusing on identity. if a parent decides they want to focus purely on the scientific/biological distinctions to avoid confusion, are they being \"unhealthy\" or \"not inclusive\" in their parenting? why is the identity side considered the more important \"correct\" way to foster emotional growth?",
